# Brand-use policy

Copyright (c) 2026 Lucas Hanson. All rights reserved except for the permissions below.

## Scope

This policy covers the hbit and Hanson BitOptik names, logos, wordmarks, favicons, app icons, branded QR artwork and other brand artwork, including their source artwork and generated copies. These materials are not covered by the MIT license for code. Fonts and other third-party materials retain their own licenses.

This is a limited permission to reproduce and display the brand assets, not an open-source license for the marks or a general trademark license. It does not assert that any mark is registered.

## Permitted uses

You may, including in commercial contexts:

- Display unmodified supplied assets to accurately refer to Lucas Hanson, hbit, Hanson BitOptik or their actual projects, including in articles, reviews, directories, documentation and screenshots.
- Copy and redistribute bundled brand assets with unmodified copies of software distributed by Lucas Hanson, including commercial redistribution. Keep this policy and applicable copyright notices with redistributed asset files; a visible credit beside each logo is not required.
- Resize proportionally and choose among supplied light, dark, monochrome and small-size variants. Ordinary rasterization or format conversion is permitted if it preserves the appearance. Keep QR codes legible and their quiet zones intact.

Follow the repository's visual usage rules. Do not stretch, recolor, redraw or re-typeset the marks. Supplied small-size variants may omit details as designed.

## Uses requiring prior written permission

Unless permitted by applicable law, obtain Lucas Hanson's written permission before:

- Using the marks as the name, logo or other source identity of your own product, service or modified software distribution.
- Suggesting sponsorship, certification, official status or endorsement that has not been granted.
- Publishing altered logos as official marks or otherwise using altered brand artwork beyond the transformations permitted above.

Code forks and modifications remain permitted by the applicable code license. For a modified distribution, remove or replace bundled branding unless you have permission to retain it; accurate references to the original project remain permitted above. Incidental marks in accurate screenshots are permitted and do not themselves require rebranding the screenshot.

## Reserved rights and lawful uses

All permissions are non-exclusive and worldwide. No ownership of the marks is transferred. No rights in the marks are granted beyond this policy. Nothing here limits fair use, nominative use or other rights and exceptions available under applicable law. No warranty is provided to the extent permitted by law.

For permission outside this policy, contact Lucas Hanson through https://links.lucashanson.dk.
